{# The serialization section, shared by every engine template that feeds the #}
{# serialization findings. Parameterized by (findings list, heading text) so #}
{# each template passes its own heading text. The body is verbatim-pinned by #}
{# the section suite in src/lib.rs — wording or formatting drift fails CI. #}
{% macro serialization_section(findings, heading, coverage) %}
{% if !findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

The following endianness and serialization patterns were recognized in this
function by static analysis — byte-swap calls, hand-rolled bit-packing chains,
and file-format signature comparisons. Where a finding is credible, express
the format with the suggested Rust type or crate instead of transliterating
the manual swaps, shifts, and masks:

{% for finding in findings %}
- **{{ finding.suggestion|safe }}** ({{ finding.kind }} pattern, confidence {{ finding.confidence }})
  Evidence: `{{ finding.evidence|safe }}`
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if !coverage.admission.is_empty() %}
{% if findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

{% endif %}
Coverage: {{ coverage.admission }}

{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}